    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="8.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIIAtr">III Atr</ref> 8.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="230" ed="#liebermann"/>And nan mann ne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIIAtr_8-1.lnote.oe.2"/> áge nænne mynetere buton cyng.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="8.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="230" ed="#liebermann"/>Et nullus habeat aliquem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IIIAtr_8-1.lnote.oe.16"/> monetarium nisi rex.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="8.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="68" ed="#robertson"/>And nan mann ne áge nænne mynetere buton cyng.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="231" ed="#liebermann"/>Und niemand als der König<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIIAtr_8-1.lnote.de.1"/> habe einen Münzer.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let no one but the king have a moneyer.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="69" ed="#robertson"/>And no-one except the king<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIIAtr_8-1.robnote.n.1"/> shall have a moneyer.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="446" ed="#whitelock"/>And no one except the king is to have a moneyer.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">H's ‘ne áge’ is written as one word ‘neáge’.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIIAtr_8-1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">230</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIIAtr_8-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">230</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">neáge <hi rend="italic">ein Wort</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">neáge as one word</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIIAtr_8-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">160</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Münze 6</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Münze 6</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIIAtr_8-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">321</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">If this is to be taken literally, the right of having moneyers possessed by certain ecclesiastics according to II As. 14, 2 was for a time withdrawn (cf. Parsons, <hi rend="italic">Brit. Numis. Journal</hi>, <hi rend="italic">Sec. Ser.</hi>, Vol. <hi rend="smallcaps">iii</hi>. p. 9). These rights were restored before the Conquest (see DB. <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi>. 179 <hi rend="italic">a</hi>, 1; <hi rend="smallcaps">ii</hi>. 117 <hi rend="italic">b</hi>).</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
